# Compose Previews

Every `@Composable` that draws UI must have a matching `@Preview` (or `@PreviewLightDark` / multipreview).

- Add a preview function next to the composable (same file), named `{Name}Preview`.
- Use `@Preview(showBackground = true)` at minimum; add dark/light or device variants when useful.
- Wire realistic sample params (fake data, theme wrapper) so the preview renders without runtime app state.
- Wrap with the app theme (`GaliusTheme` or project theme) when the composable depends on it.
- Skip preview only for non-UI composables (e.g. pure state holders, effects-only, private helpers that take no meaningful UI).
- When editing an existing composable, add or update its preview if missing or stale.
